  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Offre de services pour la r&#xE9;ponse aux Violences Bas&#xE9;es sur le Genre et Abus et Exploitation Sexuels, incluant l&#x2019;acc&#xE8;s aux services de sant&#xE9; reproductive (SR)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main aim of this $250,000 UNFPA project is to provide access to GBV services and information to flood-affected women and girls. To that end, UNFPA will create safe spaces, provide psychosocial support, distribute menstrual hygiene management kits, deploy midwives and install emergency tents to respond to sexual violence cases. Overall, UNFPA will target 26,211 people, including 10,257 women and 8,461 girls. Among those targeted, UNFPA expects to be 257 people with disabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
